{
  "_comment": "HELD-OUT evaluation corpus for the IAM privilege-escalation Sigma rule (CreateUser -> AttachUserPolicy admin within 5m). DISTINCT from data/cloudtrail/events.json (the demo/tuning set the rule was written against). Each case is a labelled mini-timeline: 'attack' cases the rule MUST fire on, 'benign' cases it must NOT. Neutral framing (no fictional org). Account 111122223333 throughout. The near-misses are the point: legitimate provisioning that LOOKS like the attack, and an attack variant that hides from a naive rule. NOTE: every event here is a CloudTrail MANAGEMENT event (IAM/STS/EC2 control-plane). S3 object-level (data-plane) reads are NOT logged by default, so a corpus that pretends GetObject exfil is always visible would be dishonest; where data-plane access matters, it is represented only as the management-plane footprint a default trail actually captures.",
